class:: RulkovMap
summary:: Raw two-state Rulkov discrete neuron map
categories:: UGens>Generators>Chaotic>Maps
related:: Guides/StochasticDynamicsUGens, Classes/Izhikevich

description::

Implements Nikolai Rulkov's discrete neuron recurrence code::x' = alpha/(1+x*x) + y:: and code::y' = y - mu*(x-sigma)::. Suitable parameters produce quiescence, spikes, or bursts without an added threshold output.

The outputs are raw state coordinates. They are not normalized audio signals and may diverge for some parameters.

Like link::Classes/Stepper::, it advances only on trigger edges; unlike Stepper, its fast and slow coordinates form a neuron model.

subsection:: Fast-slow portrait

image::rulkov-map-phase.png#The default Rulkov orbit after its transient. Fast state x is horizontal and slow state y is vertical; the long excursion corresponds to a burst cycle.::

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: trig
Advance one model iteration on a rising edge.
argument:: alpha
Fast-state nonlinearity parameter.
argument:: mu
Slow-state update coefficient.
argument:: sigma
Slow-state reference parameter.
argument:: x0
Initial fast coordinate.
argument:: y0
Initial slow coordinate.
argument:: reset
Restore initial coordinates on a rising edge.
returns:: Two audio-rate outputs: fast x and slow y.

method:: kr
Control-rate version with the same arguments and outputs.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
{ RulkovMap.ar(Impulse.ar(1000))[0] * 0.03 }.play
)
::

code::
(
{ Decay2.ar(RulkovMap.ar(Impulse.ar(800))[0] > 0, 0.001, 0.03) * 0.1 }.play
)
::

subsection:: Real-time fast-slow portrait

code::
(
SDPhaseView.open(
    "Rulkov map: fast-slow portrait",
    [-2.5, 1.5], [-3.05, -2.65],
    { RulkovMap.kr(Impulse.kr(600)) },
    { |state|
        var spike = HPZ1.kr(state[0] > 0).max(0);
        Pan2.ar(
            Decay2.ar(K2A.ar(spike), 0.001, 0.035) * SinOsc.ar(700, 0, 0.09),
            state[1].clip(-3.05, -2.65).linlin(-3.05, -2.65, -1, 1)
        )
    }
);
)
::

